Tests ability to design a beginner-friendly agent that combines planning and tool use with practical reliability patterns (retry, cache, idempotence) in a real-world domain. It also evaluates how the candidate organizes prompts and observability.

## Key Concepts
- LangChain chains and prompt templates
- AutoGen-style planning to sequence tools
- Tool usage with APIs and KB lookups
- Retry/backoff and cache strategies
- Idempotence verification and basic observability

